  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "u16-1",
      "title": "Will and going to",
      "explanation": [
        "Future: **sal** (will) or **gaan** (going to), with the main verb **at the end**.",
        "**Ek sal jou help.** = I will help you. **Ons gaan vanaand swem.** = We're going to swim tonight.",
        "New words: **bel** (call / phone), **swem** (swim), **help** (help), **vanaand** (tonight)."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "Ek sal jou môre bel.",
          "en": "I will call you tomorrow."
        },
        {
          "af": "Ons gaan vanaand braai.",
          "en": "We're going to braai tonight."
        },
        {
          "af": "Sy gaan Saterdag swem.",
          "en": "She's going to swim on Saturday."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "sal",
        "bel",
        "swem",
        "help",
        "vanaand"
      ],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "type": "order",
          "en": "I will call you tomorrow.",
          "af": "Ek sal jou môre bel."
        },
        {
          "type": "transform",
          "instruction": "Put it in the future with **sal**",
          "from": "Ek help jou.",
          "answers": [
            "Ek sal jou help."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "translate",
          "from": "en",
          "prompt": "We are going to swim tonight.",
          "answers": [
            "Ons gaan vanaand swem.",
            "Vanaand gaan ons swem."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "translate",
          "from": "af",
          "prompt": "Hy sal môre bel.",
          "answers": [
            "He will call tomorrow.",
            "He'll call tomorrow."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u16-2",
      "title": "Can, must, want, may",
      "explanation": [
        "**kan** (can), **moet** (must, have to), **wil** (want to), **mag** (may). The main verb goes to the **end**.",
        "**Ek kan swem.** **Jy moet nou gaan.** **Ek wil huis toe gaan.**",
        "Past forms: **kon, moes, wou, mog**. **Ek kon nie kom nie.** (I couldn't come.)",
        "Polite requests: **Ek wil graag…** (I'd like to…). New words: **doen** (do), **kom** (come), **kry** (get), **huiswerk** (homework)."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "Kan jy my help?",
          "en": "Can you help me?"
        },
        {
          "af": "Ek moet huiswerk doen.",
          "en": "I have to do homework."
        },
        {
          "af": "Ek wil graag 'n koffie hê.",
          "en": "I'd like a coffee."
        },
        {
          "af": "Ek kon nie kom nie.",
          "en": "I couldn't come."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        "kan",
        "moet",
        "wil",
        "mag",
        "graag",
        "doen",
        "kom",
        "huiswerk",
        "kry"
      ],
      "exercises": [
        {
          "type": "order",
          "en": "Can you help me?",
          "af": "Kan jy my help?"
        },
        {
          "type": "order",
